WEBVTT

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.540
Soft, juicy flesh, and crispy-yet-chewy skin...

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.920
It's great!

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.760
We'll be sketching outdoors today.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.270
I'll critique them later on, so do your best!

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.770
Okay!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.610
It's gotten kinda chilly.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.280
What's wrong?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.660
It just doesn't feel like fall.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.910
The leaves haven't even turned yet,

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:26.410
and I wish it'd just decide whether it wants to be hot or cold already!

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.620
Didn't you just spend all summer
complaining about how hot you were?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.670
Well...

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.300
What's up, Ryo?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.470
Ah...

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.970
It feels like summer's well and truly over, you know?

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:47.850
Yeah!

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:52.900
It's kinda sad. I don't want it to be fall yet!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.570
Oh, right.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.240
We're having a pike mackerel cookout at my place next week.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:00.820
Wanna come?

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.070
Sure!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.660
Yay! Three cheers for fall!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.160
I thought that might interest you.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.790
Why pike mackerel all of a sudden?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:13.000
My relatives are sending some next week,
so I thought I'd share.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.710
Are you sure you'll have enough left for your family?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.670
They usually send so many
that we have a hard time using them all.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.760
Really, I'm hoping you'll help us out
before our house turns into an animal shelter.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.350
Every year around this time,
the smell attracts tons of stray cats.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.060
I-I see.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.730
We'll be grilling them on a shichirin,
so they should come out pretty well.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.900
Oh, wow! I've never used one of those before!

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.530
A shichirin?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.200
It's a grill made out of porcelain.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.950
How do you cook with it?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.120
Um...

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.040
I'll figure out by next week, I guess.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.080
Grea—

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.710
No, we'll cook this time.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.580
Right, Morino?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.170
<i>That's news to me!</i>

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.550
Why are you volunteering me to—

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.680
Machiko's always the one who gets stuck cooking, right?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.180
But the food comes out better that way!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.020
I noticed when I visited over summer vacation.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.770
Not only do you slack off while she's cooking...

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.770
but you also make her do all the cleaning and chores.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.770
You're a total freeloader.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.110
Have you no mercy, Shiina?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:29.990
I think being able to try something you put
your heart into would make her really happy.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.460
<i>It's great! Kirin, you're the best!</i>

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.340
Um... Is there something—

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.220
I beg of you! Allow us to cook!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.340
<i>That polite?!</i>

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.140
Let us return the favor for once.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.970
Favor?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:50.810
Right?

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:51.350
Right!

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.060
What's wrong?

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.480
I'm just surprised.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.440
I didn't realize you two were interested in cooking.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.900
<i>That's right! Neither of us know anything about cooking!</i>

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.990
Don't worry. I'm great at cooking pike mackerel.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.120
<i>She's faking. I know it!</i>

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.420
There we go.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.300
Another hour, huh?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.840
Morning, Ryo!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.260
Hi, Kirin!

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.100
See you, Ryo!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.680
Huh? But you just got here!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.020
I'm headed to Kirin's to get ready for the cookout.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.810
Come over at around four.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.650
See you!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.990
I'm glad they're cooking for me,
but I feel kind of lonely right now.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:54.750
I wonder how the two of them are doing.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.160
What else...

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.790
It'd be handy to have Machiko here, even just for the charcoal.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.090
I guess Morino can carry enough for five people, but...

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.170
Shiina!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.840
I found the charcoal! You think this is enough?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.350
Or enough for five dozen people. That works too, I guess.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.100
I feel kinda bad not bringing Ryo along.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.810
We did want to let her take a break, though.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.690
Anyway, you told her you were great at cooking pike mackerel.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.900
What are we gonna do?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:27.860
Don't worry.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.320
I asked Tsuyuko to help.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.410
Tsuyuko? You mean the lady who looks just like you?

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.200
Yeah. She's an amazing cook.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.040
I've heard that three-star Japanese, Chinese,
and French chefs all bow down in awe to her.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.420
Sounds like she's in the wrong profession!

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.420
I wonder if Ryo will be happy?

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.550
I hope this cheers her up.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.180
She's seemed kind of down ever since Obon.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.810
I think she must be thinking of her grandma.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.560
If only she'd talk to me when she's feeling sad.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.780
I see. So she's seemed depressed lately?

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.570
Isn't that what gave you the idea for the cookout?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.280
I guess it must have been.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.160
<i>Very well, then. Let's begin.</i>

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.660
Grilled pike mackerel, as requested.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.960
Let's begin with a single fish.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.790
What, just one? Shouldn't we have a lot more if it's a party?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.130
Are you underestimating grilling with charcoal?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.840
It's the foundation of cooking pike mackerel.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.390
The process is so simple that no artifice can conceal poor work.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:37.140
It's said that Japanese cooking takes three years to learn, but grilling takes a lifetime to master.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:42.900
Grilling fish requires deft control of the flame and an intuitive sense of timing honed by experience.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.610
For pike mackerel, a fatty fish—

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.400
I'm sorry. Could you just grill the charcoal for us?

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.280
I think you mean the pike mackerel.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.570
First, the preparation.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.540
As the intestines are delicious, they do not need to be gutted.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.250
Gently sprinkle salt from a height.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.000
Hmm...

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.130
Then cut X-shaped slices in the skin.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:15.220
It will speed the cooking and add visual appeal.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.350
S-Slices?!

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.350
Oh, are you one of those people who hates touching raw fish?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.890
I-It's not like that.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:26.690
I've just never cooked fish, so I'm not really sure—

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.280
Ah, this is nice and cool.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.370
You're going to bruise it.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:43.500
They have really clear eyes.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.130
The freshness of a pike mackerel can be seen in its eyes.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.750
Those with clouded eyes will soon go bad.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.760
It's sparkling.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.270
What's wrong?

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.140
I think we just made eye contact.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.400
You're just personifying it a bit too much.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.270
Because of the smoke,

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.780
pike mackerel cannot be grilled inside,

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.110
so let's prepare the grated radish and other seasonings now.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.070
Okay!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.240
And now I must take my leave.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.660
Where are you going?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.710
Madam asked that we use the
sudachi fruit that she's growing.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.630
I'm going to harvest some.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.540
Yay, tons of fresh sudachi!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.180
And here I am.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.970
<i>Even though they said not to help, I'm still worried.</i>

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:45.560
No matter how many times I see it,
I'm still amazed by this house.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.440
Oh, hello there, Ryo!

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.730
Hello, Mrs—

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.190
Wh-What happened to your hands?!

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.530
Oh, this is just from a chemical I'm using in the fields.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:04.080
It makes the fruits grow seedless.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.160
I-Is that it?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.170
You surprised me.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.670
Oh, by the way, here. It's just rice crackers, but...

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.710
Thank you!

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.590
Would you like a box of musk melons?

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.550
How about a block of fresh ham? We have plenty of that!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.470
I couldn't accept anything that expensive!

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.930
I'll be outside all day working in the garden, but—

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.060
Oh, Tsuyuko!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.020
Yes, if there's anything you need, see Tsuyuko.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.860
H-Hello!

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.570
I'm sorry. I'm here a little bit early...

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.070
Please come in.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.960
U-Uh...

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.460
Has Kirin been giving you any trouble?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.220
No. She's been working extremely hard.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.930
I see.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.090
And you as well.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:09.350
I've heard from both Madam and the
young mistress just how hard you work.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.650
I suppose it's just that you prefer not to rely on the kindness of others,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:20.240
but there may very well be others out there who would like to do things for you.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:25.830
Kirin?!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.580
Oh, Ryo!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.330
J-Just a sec.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:36.250
I-I bumped into the table, and the pike mackerel just kinda jumped out at me, and—

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.550
No, stop! That's dangerous!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.680
We need to clean it up!

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.300
Stay back.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:46.760
But...

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.270
That's most of the fish, isn't it?

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:59.940
Three-second rule! They're fine. Just need to wash 'em off!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:07.790
Shall we bring the shichirin to the courtyard, then?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.740
Sure!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.250
All right!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.420
Let's light this fire!

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.670
Let me—

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:19.630
No way, Ryo!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.300
Just sit down and wait!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.760
O-Okay...

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.430
Next, to prepare the charcoal.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.270
Way ahead of you!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.400
See? I've jammed it in as tight as it'll fit!

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:38.360
This is...

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.780
I'm great at puzzle games!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.320
...completely out of the question.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.660
Try not to fan too hard.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.920
They smell great!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:11.680
Kirin and Shiina are both so intent.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.850
It's done!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.350
Our grilled pike mackerel is complete!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.820
What a lovely golden color!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.990
They look great!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.660
Here, Ryo!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.080
Try one!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.870
You always cook tasty things for us.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:41.840
So today, we wanted to thank you by cooking for you instead!

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:48.840
She was just kidding when she said she was great at cooking pike mackerel, but I hope you still give it a try.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:50.720
Of course!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.520
We used top-quality ingredients, so it should be fine.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.600
Timing, Shiina. Timing.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:19.830
Soft, juicy flesh, and crispy-yet-chewy skin...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.750
It's great!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:26.630
It's really wonderful. You two should have some too.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.720
Sure!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.560
The crispy, salty skin is amazing!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.480
It's way better than on a griddle!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:48.610
The smell of pike mackerel is the smell of fall.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:54.740
<i>It really is great, isn't it?</i>

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:00.040
<i>I knew food eaten with people you love tasted better,</i>

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:07.090
<i>but I'd never really thought about how food
cooked by people you love tasted better too.</i>

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.560
How is it, Tsuyuko?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.770
Miserable.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:20.770
<i>She's harsh!</i>

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.980
It's burnt. Scorched.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.400
You turned it far too often for fish.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:29.110
The cuts are too deep. You've completely killed the natural flavor of the fish.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.990
That's...

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.200
But it tasted good.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:40.250
What's most important is that you put your hearts into it.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.670
You did well.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.250
Tsuyuko...

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.670
Now that you've learned what <i>not</i> to do,
give it five more tries.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.260
The carrot-and-stick approach?!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:56.010
Am I fanning it right?

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.180
I think so.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.770
So, what do you think?

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:05.020
It's been so long since someone's cooked for me like this.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.190
It's wonderful. I'm happy.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:12.610
I do feel a little bit guilty, though.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.200
I'm sure they don't want you to feel that way.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.700
Huh?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:23.500
I think what they're really trying to tell you
is that they want you to rely on them more.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.300
Almost.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.300
Not yet! We can't turn them yet!

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:36.390
The actual results may leave something to be desired, but they're already putting such warmth into it...

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.940
You should let them help out with the housework, and talk to them when you're feeling unhappy.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:48.820
I'm sure that they'll be there for you.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.070
Tsuyuko...

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.570
And of course, it's my responsibility to teach them how.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.320
<i>She's surprisingly passionate.</i>

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.830
It's burning!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:06.380
<i>Having a meal someone cooked just for me,
for the first time in so long...</i>

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.040
Water! Water!

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.630
<i>Having people close to me whom I can rely on...</i>

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:13.010
Save the fish!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:17.430
<i>They really do so much for me.</i>

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.100
Aww.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.850
No good. It's burnt to a crisp.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.640
Ryo?

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.560
In this case, it's only skin deep.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.400
It only burned for a moment,

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:35.030
so if you just peel it back like this... There.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:38.780
Wow, you're right!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.530
It's great!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.120
Dig in!

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.220
Captain! We've got another casualty!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.340
Never mind that.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.470
Carry on!

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.760
The water suddenly—

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.980
Young mistress! Your raincoat!

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:06.560
Roger!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.060
Um...

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.650
Dishwashing is the simplest task in cooking.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.820
If they can't handle this,
they'll never amount to anything!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.070
O-Okay...

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:24.700
Captain! We've been ambushed
by the dishes in the cabinet!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.000
Captain...

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:37.630
Put them away later! Twenty-eight percent of the dishes are still dirty!

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.300
Young mistress, take your cold medicine immediately!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.610
I said not to—

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.990
L-Let me at least clean this up!

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:04.370
It's driving me nuts! I want to help at least a little bit!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:09.370
I see. Perhaps that's simply the cross you must bear.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:12.880
Captain!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.640
I think I got most of it out.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:29.140
Kirin? I couldn't completely get the smell of the smoke out,

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.350
so you should take it to the dry clean...

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.450
Ryo?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:48.790
Oh, did I wake you up?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:51.210
What are you doing?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:57.550
They gave me the leftover pike mackerel, so I thought I'd make some with ginger, served with mixed rice.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.760
Wait! Teach me how to make it!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.340
I don't mind cooking this time.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.890
No! Let me do it!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:12.230
I want to be good at cooking pike mackerel for real!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:16.820
Let's cook together, then.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:20.440
No! Today's your day off!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:26.830
Please, let me help! I want to touch the fresh pike mackerel this time!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.040
You're that desperate to?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:32.580
<i>I want to let Kirin do something for me,</i>

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.840
<i>but cooking together like this is fun too.</i>

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:52.350
<i>Cooking food I love, with someone I love...</i>

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:03.280
This weekend was so much fun!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:07.990
Grilling is great, but the mixed rice came out nice too.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:09.990
I'm glad you enjoyed yourself.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.620
I guess I'm still a little hungry.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:16.830
Even at school, I couldn't stop thinking about the pike mackerel,

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:22.010
and when I did it was like I could actually smell it!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:28.930
Anyway, see you next week!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.360
R-Ryo?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.110
I see pike mackerel isn't to be trifled with.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.950
Even the deodorizer wasn't enough.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.740
It smells like pike mackerel...

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:58.750
Apologize to the people next to you on the train for me.

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:46.940
You look like you're in a good mood today, Ryo.

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:49.610
Yeah! Believe it or not, Kirin cooked—

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:51.860
Wait, I can't tell you!

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:54.620
But I can give you a hint.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.790
A special treat just for me, for lunch on field day...

00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:00.500
That's all I can say!

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:03.200
That doesn't tell me anything, but I think I know.

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.000
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.050
Flaky and Toasty!
